@rekram1-node 

biome's lsp is not currently supported, and when used in the `opencode + omo` scenario, there will be an exception when calling `lsp_diagnostics` on the file (if there is an error syntax, it will return to normal), but when I use `opencode debug lsp xxx`, I can call lsp normally to get the error information. This is my current biome configuration
```
{
  // Project-level OpenCode config (JSONC).
  // Temporary custom Biome LSP: remove when OpenCode ships built-in Biome LSP.
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "lsp": {
    // Disable built-in JS/TS diagnostics to avoid duplicate lint reports.
    "typescript": {
      "disabled": true
    },
    "eslint": {
      "disabled": true
    },
    "custom-biome": {
      // Use project-local biome from node_modules via npx.
      "command": [
        "npx",
        "biome",
        "lsp-proxy"
      ],
      "extensions": [
        ".js",
        ".jsx",
        ".mjs",
        ".cjs",
        ".ts",
        ".tsx",
        ".mts",
        ".cts"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

I am using now https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/pull/15710 the whole week - very helpful. IMHO better than the current `/diff` implementation in codex, so I think it's a good start. 

Once merged, I would like to add a comment feature so I can send a review to the coding agent. 

